{"id": "EUVD-2026-100396", "enisaUuid": "dab0df8d-aea5-38b4-acdb-19481412fe12", "description": "An elevation of privilege vulnerability exists in the Network Driver Interface Specification (NDIS) when ndis.sys fails to check the length of a buffer prior to copying memory to it.\nTo exploit the vulnerability, in a local attack scenario, an attacker could run a specially crafted application to elevate the attacker's privilege level. An attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability could run processes in an elevated context. However, an attacker must first gain access to the local system with the ability to execute a malicious application in order to exploit this vulnerability.\nThe security update addresses the vulnerability by changing how ndis.sys validates buffer length.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T19:01:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T22:26:21", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H/E:U/RL:O/RC:C", "references": ["https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-105007"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6mcc-m77g-xpcv", "CVE-2026-105007"], "assigner": "microsoft", "epss": 0.77, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "119c937c-2e78-3d14-86a8-95f4a1bb3bb3", "product": {"name": "Windows 11 version 26H1", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "10.0.28000.0 <10.0.28000.3231"}, {"id": "153494f5-283c-3d3f-bb18-a79c3c660698", "product": {"name": "Windows Server 2019 (Server Core installation)", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "10.0.17763.0 <10.0.17763.9376"}, {"id": "1b54b164-589e-35e8-b5a9-8364ac591291", "product": {"name": "Windows 10 Version 1607", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "10.0.14393.0 <10.0.14393.9612"}, {"id": "3aee7161-6c05-3833-958e-1cd9fa9e7e56", "product": {"name": "Windows Server 2012", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "6.2.9200.0 <6.2.9200.26434"}, {"id": "3ce710e7-9b11-3b4f-a361-0e5093a6588c", "product": {"